h('3. Exact address-color restriction')
p('<b>Proposition.</b> Let H_A be any finite address space and H_C=(C^3) tensor (C^3) tensor (C^3), carrying the same fundamental SU(3) action on each factor. Let P project onto the common kernel of the eight Q_a. If a density operator Omega satisfies Omega=(I_A tensor P) Omega (I_A tensor P), then P=|S><S| and Omega=sigma_A tensor |S><S| for a unique address density operator sigma_A.')
p('<b>Proof.</b> The two diagonal traceless generators require equal occupation of all three colors, leaving only the six permutations of rgb. For each pair of colors, the raising operator maps two permutations differing by their exchange to the same repeated-color output. Its vanishing forces opposite coefficients. These transposition relations connect all six permutations, fixing their coefficients up to an overall amplitude and permutation parity. Direct substitution verifies the resulting |S> is annihilated by every Q_a, so the kernel has dimension one. Expand Omega=sum_nm |n><m| tensor C_nm. Rank-one support gives C_nm=P C_nm P=c_nm P. Hence Omega=sigma_A tensor P. Positivity and unit trace pass to sigma_A; partial trace gives uniqueness.')
p('For address observable B and color observable C, expectations therefore factor as Tr(sigma_A B) times &lt;S|C|S&gt;. Address-controlled collective transformations U_n tensor U_n tensor U_n with U_n in SU(3) leave |S> fixed and cannot encode different address labels into this sector. A prospective decoder that deletes address labels cannot reconstruct them from this fixed color state. Exact support is stronger than zero mean charge; omitted gluon, flavor or spatial factors can change the applicable representation. Spin, confinement, binding, a particle spectrum and arithmetic selection of SU(3) remain open.')
h('4. The implemented release decision')
p('The three findings answer one packaging problem: which interpretation can accompany the actual Stage-3 outputs? A reproducible component replay is needed to establish the measured order dependence; dependency inspection establishes that color success does not supply arithmetic sensitivity; the rank-one proof establishes the declared color interface limit. claim_gate.py consumes audit_results.json, dependency_results.json and a JSON list of requested claim identifiers. Its predicates are explicit, source-specific release policy, not a new universal criterion of physics.')
table([['Requested claim / integration case','Delivered gate result'],['Component replay; declared color consistency; exact three-factor constraint','ACCEPT; all three are supported under their stated contracts'],['Add arithmetic_derivation_of_color','REJECT despite the original 36 checks passing: the audited routine has no arithmetic input'],['Add order_independent_component_decoder','REJECT using the actual nonzero assembly TV'],['Request an unknown claim, e.g. confinement_derived','REJECT: no declared supporting contract']])
p('The code returns process exit status 0 for an accepted requested claim set and 2 for a rejected one. The concrete development decision is therefore implemented: this release can carry its demonstrated conditional results, while an automated review/export step refuses the unsupported stronger interpretations. It does not establish that the original project made those interpretations. The factorization proof supplies a further rule for future decoder design; it does not prescribe a new physical coupling. Adding more tests of the same singlet would not establish such a coupling.')
p('All four integration scenarios pass their expected acceptance/rejection conditions. The original 36-check suite and four dependency checks remain separately reported. The utility is a working claim boundary for this release, rather than novelty of the underlying representation theory or a claim that test counts establish physical adequacy.')
page()
h('5. Verification results and reproduction')
table([['Diagnostic','Recorded result'],['Original replay/color suite','36 / 36 pass'],['Source-dependency suite','4 / 4 pass'],['Release-gate integration scenarios','4 / 4 behave as specified'],['Common kernel dimension','1, numerical and exact symbolic'],['Maximum total-generator action','0 in the recorded original run'],['Generator Gram / commutator errors',f"{e['gram_error']:.3e} / {e['commutator_closure_error']:.3e}"],['Collective SU(3) rotation error, 32 trials',f"{e['collective_SU3_rotation_max_error_32_cases']:.3e}"],['Joint-state factorization error',f"{e['projected_joint_state_factorization_error']:.3e}"],['rgb / one-site phase negative-control charge norms','0.707106781 / 0.816496581']])
p('The exact symbolic calculation uses nonzero rescalings of the generators to remove radicals; the common kernel and signed integer singlet vector are checked without numerical tolerance. The joint-state test projects a seeded positive 6-address by 27-color density operator into the exact singlet sector and compares it with the product of its address marginal and the singlet projector. Negative controls violate the color constraint and are detected. Checks overlap and are not independent physical observations.')
p('The exact v0.7 manuscript and companion sources are archived at <link href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23497198" color="blue">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23497198</link>. RELEASE.json identifies this PDF, scientific scripts, source manifest and reference outputs with SHA-256. SOURCE_SHA256.json is checked before scientific execution. The unchanged upstream source has commit 9d9daf21154e46e55b9fd0fd461c7c070156ab94; its Stage-3 code and calculations/wrra_m_0_9 are reproduced in source/.')
eq('python3 -m venv .venv\n.venv/bin/python -m pip install numpy==2.3.5 scipy==1.17.0 sympy==1.14.0\n.venv/bin/python audit.py\n.venv/bin/python dependency_audit.py\n.venv/bin/python claim_gate.py')
p('Recorded Python: 3.12.14. Reruns overwrite their result JSON files; preserve reference bytes for release-hash checks. Different runtime metadata or numerical libraries can change output hashes. Absolute fraction/share tolerances are 2 x 10^-12, historical mean-count tolerance 2 x 10^-10, matrix tolerance 10^-12 and numerical kernel threshold 10^-10; symbolic tests use exact zero. Gate acceptance requires the declared audit statuses and source-specific evidence contracts. Known inputs and reproduced values remain legitimate model-construction and consistency results. This note does not require a new observational prediction to state its bounded contribution.')
h('Conclusion')
p('The frozen particle/component replay is reproducible and order dependent. Its supplied color test preserves the declared singlet but consumes no arithmetic state, and its exact three-factor singlet sector cannot retain address distinctions. The delivered release gate makes those findings usable in the actual package: it accepts supported conditional statements and rejects stronger unsupported interpretations. This is a compact reproducibility and technical implementation report; general physical completion remains outside its claim.')
